//1.Error description and what it means  
/** 
1. What the error means (simple terms)
  -A StackOverflowError happens when your program keeps calling the same method over and over without stopping. Think of it like someone falling into an endless loop of stairs — eventually, they run out of space. In your case, the factorial function never reached a stopping point, so Java’s memory stack filled up.
 */
